就像他的，他的心脏再也撑不下去了。

00:36:54.344 --> 00:36:59.076
And it was, and it was like one of those things where everyone wanted it to work.
而且，这就像是那种所有人都希望出现奇迹的情况。

00:36:59.076 --> 00:37:01.296
And they kept pushing to make it work.
大家都在拼命维持，想尽一切办法。

00:37:01.296 --> 00:37:06.437
And we both kind of knew like it's done, like it's just, it's just done working for you.
但我们心里其实都很清楚，一切都结束了，它就是，它就是不再为你工作了。

00:37:06.230 --> 00:37:08.789
like it doesn't want to work for you anymore and there's something more to do.
就好像它不再愿意为你跳动了，而你已经无能为力了。

00:37:09.829 --> 00:37:11.944
And that what I was really hard.
那段经历真的非常艰难。

00:37:11.944 --> 00:37:18.223
And it felt like it felt like a decision that we made, but it was something that had to happen.
感觉这好像是我们作出的决定，但其实那是不得不发生的事情。

00:37:18.223 --> 00:37:24.633
Because I don't think any doctor wants to say to a 43-year-old man like, okay, I guess that's it.
因为我觉得没有任何一个医生会想对一个43岁的男人说：“好吧，我想就这样了。”

00:37:24.633 --> 00:37:26.285
No one wants to say that.
没有人会想说这种话。

00:37:26.285 --> 00:37:30.184
They want to fight for you and try to do whatever they can.
他们想为你战斗，想尽一切可能去尝试。

00:37:30.184 --> 00:37:40.230
But you know, it's something my husband said to me before I, what I'm very grateful for is that we had time to talk to each other before he passed away.
但你知道，我非常感激的是，在我丈夫去世前，他曾跟我说过一句话，那就是我们在他离世前还有时间交谈。

00:37:41.030 --> 00:37:47.349
And one of the things he said to me was, you know, he felt like his purpose was to have our child.
他对我说的其中一件事是，你知道，他觉得他的人生目标就是拥有我们的孩子。

00:37:48.070 --> 00:37:51.429
He felt like that was, that was the point of like him being here.
他觉得这才是，这就是他来到这里的意义。

00:37:52.389 --> 00:37:57.870
And he went through like a lot of times in his life where he was like depressed a little bit and got out of it.
他的人生中曾有很多时候感到有点沮丧，但后来都挺过来了。

00:37:57.870 --> 00:38:01.030
And when he met me, he was like a really high point in his life.
当他遇到我时，正处于他人生中非常高光的时刻。

00:38:01.030 --> 00:38:08.789
He was doing really well in his 30s, and he felt like I'm going to try to do something for myself and not worry about my mortality.
他在三十多岁时状态极佳，他觉得自己要为自己做点什么，而不要总去担心自己的生命长短。

00:38:08.789 --> 00:38:18.750
And we built this life for eight years, and I felt like that's maybe what he was supposed to do is just kind of find that time to embrace life and his adulthood.
我们一起构建了八年的生活，我觉得这可能就是他该做的事——去寻找那个拥抱生活和成年人生的时刻。

00:38:18.750 --> 00:38:28.349
But anyway, and we have this amazing, amazing, healthy kid, so I, you know, I can't, but yeah, but thank you.
不管怎样，我们拥有了一个如此惊艳、如此健康的孩子，所以我，你知道，我不能，但是，是的，谢谢你。

00:38:28.349 --> 00:38:29.510
Thank you, Craig, for sharing that again.
克雷格，谢谢你再次分享这些。

00:38:29.510 --> 00:38:40.170
I'm so glad that he got to experience the gift of you and the gift of your child and that he felt that was the meaning in his life because, of course, that is the beauty and meaning of life.
我很高兴他曾体验过拥有你的馈赠以及拥有你们孩子的馈赠，并且他认为这就是他生命的意义，因为这当然就是生命的美丽与意义所在。

00:38:40.170 --> 00:38:43.829
And I'm so glad that he got that and, you know, I'm so glad he got that with you.
我很高兴他得到了这一切，你知道的，我也很高兴他是和你一起得到了这一切。

00:38:43.829 --> 00:39:02.289
I heard his story years ago about, um, Meryl Streep was with for years with the actor John Kazale, who was this toweringly great American character actors and dog day afternoon, godfather, And he was just so respected among actors, and they were very much in love.
