00:39:02.289 --> 00:39:10.769
And he, I think, had a brain tumor or something, and he had a death that was like swift but gave them enough time to do what you were talking about.
我记得他好像得了脑瘤什么的，他的离去很突然，但又给了他们足够的时间去做你刚才说的那种事。

00:39:10.769 --> 00:39:11.769
Yeah.
对。

00:39:11.769 --> 00:39:23.690
And I know another actor whose dear friends with her, I never met her, but he told me that he ran into her in New York while John Kazale was dying.
我知道另一个和她是非常要好的朋友的演员——我从没见过她——他告诉我，当约翰·卡扎雷垂危时，他在纽约遇到了她。

00:39:23.690 --> 00:39:35.170
And he asked how she was doing, he knew she was going through this and she said, it's the saddest thing in the world, but I have never been so present with anyone in my life.
他问她最近怎么样，他知道她正在经历这一切，而她说：“这是世界上最悲伤的事，但我一生中从未像现在这样如此专注地活在当下。”

00:39:35.170 --> 00:39:46.070
Like just the time that they were, you know, it felt like they had entered into a timeless flow state together where they weren't even bound by time anymore, you know?
就像他们相处的那段时间，你知道的，感觉他们一起进入了一种永恒的流动状态，甚至不再受时间的束缚了，你知道吗？

00:39:46.070 --> 00:40:13.429
And I think sometimes we mistake longevity for like that it's more meaningful the longer you get, but that's not necessarily true, you know, that eight years together can be more, you know, filled with meaning and import than, you know, than a 50 year marriage where you're not talking about much, you know, you're not really talking about all the real stuff.
我想有时我们会误以为在一起的时间越长就意味着越有意义，但这并不一定正确，你知道的，在一起八年所包含的意义和分量，可能比那种彼此不再深入交流、不再谈论真正重要之事的五十年婚姻还要深厚，你知道吗？

00:40:13.429 --> 00:40:24.190
But my wife, Jordana, who you've probably heard on the show, the questions and observations from a clinical psychologist who's never seen how my mother also happens to be married to Josh.
不过我的妻子乔丹娜——你可能在节目里听过她作为一名从未看过这部剧的临床心理学家的提问和观察，她同时也是乔希的妻子。

00:40:24.190 --> 00:40:25.190
Yeah.
是的。

00:40:25.190 --> 00:40:39.949
So she's a clinical psychologist and her PhD thesis was on the connection between love and death and how a more present awareness of our mortality increases intimacy.
她是一名临床心理学家，她的博士论文是关于爱与死亡之间的联系，以及对我们终有一死的更深刻意识如何增进亲密感。

00:40:39.949 --> 00:40:58.869
So I imagine that you and your husband were just at this kind of achingly intimate time in those moments before, but she also introduced me to this quote from John Fowls, a novelist who said, death is rather like a certain kind of lecturer.
所以我想象你和你的丈夫在之前的那些时刻里，正处于这种痛彻心扉的亲密时刻，但她也向我介绍了约翰·福尔斯（一位小说家）的一句名言，他说：“死亡其实有点像某种讲师。”

00:40:58.869 --> 00:41:03.389
